{"content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Why Is the Sky Blue? · 天空为什么是蓝色的?</title>
<meta name="description" content="A bilingual (English / Simplified Chinese) three-level explanation of why the sky is blue.">
<style>
  /* ---------- Design tokens ---------- */
  :root{
    --sky-1:#eaf3fb; --sky-2:#cfe4f6; --sky-3:#7fb2e0; --sky-4:#2f6ea8; --sky-5:#16405f;
    --ink:#16202b; --ink-soft:#41556b; --paper:#ffffff; --bg:#f4f8fc;
    --rule:#d9e5f0; --accent:#2f6ea8;
    --zh-font:"PingFang SC","Hiragino Sans GB","Microsoft YaHei","Noto Sans CJK SC","Source Han Sans SC","Songti SC",serif;
    --en-font:ui-serif,"Iowan Old Style","Palatino Linotype",Palatino,Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;
    --sans:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
    --mono:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,"Liberation Mono",monospace;
    --maxw:1180px;
    --radius:14px;
    --gap:clamp(14px,2vw,28px);
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){
    :root{
      --ink:#e6eef6; --ink-soft:#a9c0d4; --paper:#111b25; --bg:#0a121a;
      --rule:#1f3141; --accent:#79b4e8;
      --sky-1:#0f1c28; --sky-2:#132433; --sky-3:#2d5f8c; --sky-4:#79b4e8; --sky-5:#cfe4f6;
    }
  }

  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box}
  html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}
  body{
    margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink);
    font-family:var(--en-font); font-size:17px; line-height:1.68;
    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
    background-image:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--sky-1) 0%,transparent 380px);
  }
  [lang="zh"]{font-family:var(--zh-font); line-height:1.85; letter-spacing:.01em}

  /* ---------- Progress + header ---------- */
  #progress{position:fixed;inset:0 auto auto 0;height:3px;width:0;background:var(--accent);z-index:60;transition:width .1s linear}

  header.top{
    position:sticky;top:0;z-index:50;
    background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--bg) 82%,transparent);
    backdrop-filter:saturate(140%) blur(10px);
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  @supports not (backdrop-filter:blur(2px)){header.top{background:var(--bg)}}
  .top-inner{max-width:var(--maxw);margin:0 auto;padding:14px var(--gap)}
  .titles{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:.4em 1em}
  .titles h1{margin:0;font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.4vw,1.6rem);letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .titles h1 .zh{font-family:var(--zh-font);color:var(--ink-soft);font-weight:500}
  .titles .tag{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--ink-soft)}

  .controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 14px;margin-top:12px;align-items:center}
  .seg{display:inline-flex;background:var(--sky-1);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:999px;padding:3px;gap:2px}
  .seg button{
    font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink-soft);
    background:transparent;border:0;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 13px;cursor:pointer;
    transition:background .15s,color .15s;white-space:nowrap;
  }
  .seg button:hover{color:var(--ink)}
  .seg button[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--accent);color:#fff}
  @media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.seg button[aria-pressed="true"]{color:#08131d}}
  .seg button[aria-pressed="true"][lang="zh"]{font-family:var(--zh-font)}
  .seg-label{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-right:2px}
  .spacer{flex:1 1 auto}
  .ghost{
    font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink-soft);
    background:transparent;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:999px;padding:6px 13px;cursor:pointer
  }
  .ghost:hover{color:var(--ink);border-color:var(--accent)}

  /* ---------- Layout ---------- */
  main{max-width:var(--maxw);margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(18px,3vw,40px) var(--gap) 40px}

  .level{margin:0 0 clamp(30px,5vw,64px);scroll-margin-top:150px}
  .level-head{
    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin:0 0 18px;
    padding:14px 18px;border-radius:var(--radius);
    background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--sky-2),var(--sky-1));
    border:1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .badge{
    flex:0 0 auto;width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;
    background:var(--accent);color:#fff;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.badge{color:#08131d}}
  .level-head h2{margin:0;font-size:1.18rem;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .level-head .sub{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.74rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .level-head .zh-title{font-family:var(--zh-font);font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--ink-soft);font-weight:500}

  .pairs{display:grid;gap:1px;background:var(--rule);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden}
  .pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;background:var(--paper)}
  .cell{padding:clamp(16px,2.2vw,26px);min-width:0}
  .cell + .cell{border-left:1px solid var(--rule)}
  .cell[lang="zh"]{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--sky-1) 45%,var(--paper))}
  @supports not (backdrop-filter:blur(2px)){.cell[lang="zh"]{background:var(--sky-1)}}

  body[data-view="en"] .cell[lang="zh"],
  body[data-view="zh"] .cell[lang="en"]{display:none}
  body[data-view="en"] .pair,
  body[data-view="zh"] .pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}

  .cell h3{margin:0 0 .5em;font-size:1.02rem;line-height:1.4}
  .cell[lang="zh"] h3{font-family:var(--zh-font);font-weight:700}
  .cell p{margin:0 0 .85em}
  .cell p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .cell ul,.cell ol{margin:0 0 .85em;padding-left:1.35em}
  .cell li{margin:0 0 .5em}
  .cell li:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .cell :is(h3,p,li) code,.formula{
    font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.92em;background:var(--sky-1);
    border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:6px;padding:.08em .38em;white-space:nowrap;
  }
  .formula{display:block;padding:10px 12px;margin:0 0 .9em;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.6}
  .lead{font-size:1.08em;font-weight:600;color:var(--sky-5)}
  @media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.lead{color:var(--sky-5)}}
  .callout{
    border-left:3px solid var(--accent);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--sky-2) 55%,var(--paper));
    padding:12px 14px;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;
  }
  @supports not (backdrop-filter:blur(2px)){.callout{background:var(--sky-1)}}
  .kicker{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--accent);display:block;margin-bottom:.35em}

  /* reveal on scroll */
  .pair{opacity:0;transform:translateY(10px)}
  .pair.in{opacity:1;transform:none;transition:opacity .45s ease,transform .45s ease}
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.pair{opacity:1;transform:none}.pair.in{transition:none}}

  /* ---------- Narrow screens: stack ---------- */
  @media (max-width:860px){
    body{font-size:16px}
    .pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .cell + .cell{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}
    .cell[lang="zh"]{border-top:2px solid var(--accent)}
  }

  /* ---------- Footer ---------- */
  footer{max-width:var(--maxw);margin:0 auto;padding:0 var(--gap) 48px;color:var(--ink-soft);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem}
  footer .keys{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 14px;margin-top:8px}
  kbd{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.72rem;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-bottom-width:2px;border-radius:5px;padding:1px 6px;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink)}

  /* ---------- Print ---------- */
  @media print{
    header.top,#progress,.ghost{display:none!important}
    body{background:#fff;color:#000;font-size:11pt}
    .pair{break-inside:avoid}
    .pair,.pair.in{opacity:1;transform:none}
    .level{break-before:auto}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body data-view="both" data-level="all">

<div id="progress" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<header class="top">
  <div class="top-inner">
    <div class="titles">
      <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue? <span class="zh" lang="zh">天空为什么是蓝色的?</span></h1>
      <span class="tag">Three levels · one phenomenon</span>
    </div>

    <div class="controls">
      <span class="seg-label">Level</span>
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Select audience level">
        <button type="button" data-level="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
        <button type="button" data-level="1" aria-pressed="false">1 · Age 3</button>
        <button type="button" data-level="2" aria-pressed="false">2 · High school</button>
        <button type="button" data-level="3" aria-pressed="false">3 · PhD</button>
      </div>

      <span class="seg-label">Language</span>
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Select language view">
        <button type="button" data-view="both" aria-pressed="true">Both</button>
        <button type="button" data-view="en" aria-pressed="false">EN</button>
        <button type="button" data-view="zh" lang="zh" aria-pressed="false">中</button>
      </div>

      <span class="spacer"></span>
      <button type="button" class="ghost" id="top-btn">↑ Top</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="main"></main>

<footer>
  <p>Rayleigh scattering · σ ∝ λ⁻⁴ · blue (450 nm) scatters ≈ 4.4× more than red (650 nm).</p>
  <p class="keys">
    <span><kbd>1</kbd><kbd>2</kbd><kbd>3</kbd> jump to level</span>
    <span><kbd>0</kbd> show all</span>
    <span><kbd>L</kbd> cycle language</span>
    <span><kbd>J</kbd>/<kbd>K</kbd> next / previous section</span>
  </p>
</footer>

<script>
/* ============================================================
   Content model — each block is one paired row (EN cell | ZH cell).
   Keeping both languages in the same object guarantees the
   columns stay aligned section-by-section.
   ============================================================ */
const LEVELS = [
  {
    n:1, en:"For a 3-Year-Old", zh:"讲给 3 岁小朋友听", sub:"toddlers",
    blocks:[
      { lead:true,
        en:"<strong>The sky is blue because sunlight plays a hiding game.</strong>",
        zh:"<strong>天空是蓝色的,是因为阳光在玩捉迷藏。</strong>" },

      { en:"<p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of all the colors of the rainbow — red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and violet — all squeezed together.</p>",
        zh:"<p>阳光看起来是白色的,但它其实是由彩虹的所有颜色挤在一起组成的——红、橙、黄、绿、蓝、紫。</p>" },

      { en:"<h3>The air blanket</h3><p>Above our heads there's a big blanket of air. Air is full of tiny, tiny bits that we can't see. When the sunlight comes zooming down through the blanket, the blue color bumps into all those tiny bits and <strong>scatters</strong> — it bounces all over the place, in every direction.</p>",
        zh:"<h3>空气被子</h3><p>我们头顶上盖着一床大大的“空气被子”。空气里满是看不见的小小颗粒。当阳光嗖地一下冲进这床被子时,蓝色光就撞到了那些小颗粒上,然后<strong>散射</strong>开了——到处乱弹,朝哪个方向弹的都有。</p>" },

      { en:"<h3>Red and yellow go straight through</h3><p>Red and yellow light don't bump around much. They just go straight through, right down to the ground.</p>",
        zh:"<h3>红和黄直接穿过来</h3><p>红光和黄光不怎么碰撞,它们直接就穿过来了,一直落到地面上。</p>" },

      { en:"<h3>Blue bounces everywhere</h3><p>But the blue light gets bounced everywhere, so when you look up <em>anywhere</em> in the sky, some of that bounced-up blue light lands in your eyes. That's why the whole sky looks blue!</p>",
        zh:"<h3>蓝色到处乱弹</h3><p>可是蓝色光被弹得到处都是,所以不管你抬头看天空的哪个地方,总有一些被弹起来的蓝色光跑进你的眼睛里。这就是为什么整片天空看起来都是蓝的!</p>" },

      { en:"<h3>Sunset at bedtime</h3><p>And at bedtime, when the Sun goes low, its light has to travel through <em>lots</em> more air. By the time it gets to you, the blue has all bounced away and only the warm red and orange colors are left. That's a sunset. 🌅</p>",
        zh:"<h3>睡觉时的日落</h3><p>到了该睡觉的时候,太阳落得很低很低,它的光要穿过<strong>好多好多</strong>层的空气才能到你眼睛里。等它到达时,蓝色早就弹光了,只剩下暖暖的红颜色和橙颜色。那就是日落呀。🌅</p>" }
    ]
  },

  {
    n:2, en:"For a High School Student", zh:"讲给高中生听", sub:"high school",
    blocks:[
      { kicker:{en:"The short version",zh:"简要版"},
        en:"<p>Sunlight is a mix of all visible wavelengths. Molecules in the atmosphere (mostly N<sub>2</sub> and O<sub>2</sub>) scatter this light, and they scatter short wavelengths <strong>much</strong> more strongly than long ones. Blue light (~450 nm) gets scattered roughly 4–5× more strongly than red light (~650 nm), so the diffuse glow you see when you look away from the Sun is dominated by blue.</p>",
        zh:"<p>阳光是各种可见波长的混合。大气中的分子(主要是 N<sub>2</sub> 和 O<sub>2</sub>)会散射这些光,而且它们对短波长的散射<strong>远</strong>比对长波长的散射强。蓝光(约 450 nm)被散射的强度大约是红光(约 650 nm)的 4–5 倍,所以当你把视线移开太阳、看天空的其他部分时,那种弥漫的光晕主要由蓝色构成。</p>" },

      { kicker:{en:"Rayleigh scattering",zh:"瑞利散射"},
        en:"<p>When light's oscillating electric field hits a molecule, it shakes the molecule's electron cloud, inducing an oscillating dipole. That dipole re-radiates. If the particle is much smaller than the wavelength of light (d ≲ λ/10 — true for O<sub>2</sub>/N<sub>2</sub>, ~0.15 nm vs. ~500 nm), the scattering cross-section is:</p><code class="formula">σ ∝ (1/λ⁴) · ((n² − 1)/(n² + 2))² · V²</code>",
        zh:"<p>当光的振荡电场作用到分子上时,会晃动分子的电子云,诱导出一个振荡电偶极子。这个偶极子会再辐射。当粒子远小于光的波长时(d ≲ λ/10——对 O<sub>2</sub>/N<sub>2</sub> 成立,分子约 0.15 nm,而光约 500 nm),散射截面为:</p><code class="formula">σ ∝ (1/λ⁴) · ((n² − 1)/(n² + 2))² · V²</code>" },

      { en:"<p>Two things matter here:</p><ol><li><strong>The λ⁻⁴ dependence.</strong> This is the headline result. Halve the wavelength → 16× the scattering.<ul><li>Blue, 450 nm: relative scattering strength ≈ 1.0</li><li>Red, 650 nm: (450/650)⁴ ≈ 0.23 → about 4.3× weaker</li></ul></li><li><strong>The (n² − 1)/(n² + 2) factor</strong>, which measures how polarizable the molecule is. No polarizability, no scattering.</li></ol>",
        zh:"<p>这里有两点关键:</p><ol><li><strong>λ⁻⁴ 依赖关系。</strong>这是最重要的结论。波长减半 → 散射增强 16 倍。<ul><li>蓝光,450 nm:相对散射强度 ≈ 1.0</li><li>红光,650 nm:(450/650)⁴ ≈ 0.23 → 弱约 4.3 倍</li></ul></li><li><strong>(n² − 1)/(n² + 2) 这个因子</strong>,它衡量分子被极化的难易程度。没有极化率,就没有散射。</li></ol>" },

      { kicker:{en:"“Then why isn't the sky violet?”",zh:"“那天空为什么不是紫色的?”"},
        en:"<p>Violet scatters even more than blue, so this is the right question to ask. Three reasons:</p><ul><li><strong>The Sun emits less violet.</strong> The solar spectrum peaks in the green-yellow (~500 nm) and drops off steeply in the violet.</li><li><strong>Your eyes aren't equal-opportunity detectors.</strong> The S-cones (short-wavelength) are far less numerous than M- and L-cones, and the S-cone response actually falls off sharply below ~440 nm.</li><li><strong>Color mixing.</strong> The blue and green light that <em>does</em> scatter strongly, plus the residual red leaking through, mixes in your visual system to “white-ish blue” (cyan-blue) rather than pure violet.</li></ul>",
        zh:"<p>紫光的散射比蓝光更强,所以这是个问得很好的问题。原因有三:</p><ul><li><strong>太阳发出的紫光本来就少。</strong>太阳光谱的峰值在黄绿光区(约 500 nm),在紫端急剧下降。</li><li><strong>你的眼睛并不是“一视同仁”的探测器。</strong>S 视锥(短波长)的数量远少于 M 和 L 视锥,而且 S 视锥的响应在约 440 nm 以下本身就急剧衰减。</li><li><strong>颜色混合。</strong>同样被强烈散射的蓝光和绿光,再加上漏过来的那部分剩余红光,在你的视觉系统中混合成“偏白的蓝”(青蓝),而不是纯紫。</li></ul>" },

      { kicker:{en:"Related payoffs",zh:"相关的延伸结论"},
        en:"<ul><li><strong>Sunsets are red:</strong> at low elevation the light path through the atmosphere is long (tens of times the zenith path), so the short wavelengths are almost entirely scattered <em>out</em> of your line of sight, leaving red/orange.</li><li><strong>Clouds are white:</strong> droplets are ~10 µm — much bigger than λ. Scattering becomes nearly wavelength-independent (Mie/geometric regime), so all colors scatter equally.</li><li><strong>The sky is polarized:</strong> scattered light is linearly polarized perpendicular to the scattering plane, max at 90° from the Sun. That's how bees navigate, and why a rotating polarizing filter darkens parts of a sky photo.</li></ul>",
        zh:"<ul><li><strong>日落为什么是红的:</strong>太阳高度角低时,光穿过大气的路径很长(是天顶路径的数十倍),短波长几乎被完全散射<em>出</em>你的视线,只剩下红和橙。</li><li><strong>云为什么是白的:</strong>云滴约 10 µm——远大于波长 λ。散射几乎与波长无关(米氏散射/几何光学区),所以各种颜色被等量散射。</li><li><strong>天空光是偏振的:</strong>散射光沿垂直于散射平面的方向线偏振,在距太阳 90° 的方向偏振度最大。蜜蜂据此导航;旋转偏振镜能让天空照片的某些部分变暗,也是这个道理。</li></ul>" }
    ]
  },

  {
    n:3, en:"For a Physics PhD", zh:"讲给物理学博士听", sub:"graduate",
    blocks:[
      { kicker:{en:"Framework",zh:"理论框架"},
        en:"<p>Treat the atmosphere's refractive index as <code>n = 1 + δ</code>, δ ≈ 3×10⁻⁴ at STP. Rayleigh scattering is then scattering by thermally induced fluctuations in δ, and the total intensity in a column of air is <em>not</em> the incoherent sum over N independent molecules — you have to account for the fact that a homogeneous medium would scatter nothing at all, since the forward amplitude exactly cancels the incident beam and destructive interference kills everything else. Density fluctuations break that cancellation.</p>",
        zh:"<p>把大气的折射率写成 <code>n = 1 + δ</code>,在标准温压条件下 δ ≈ 3×10⁻⁴。于是瑞利散射本质上就是由 δ 的热致涨落引起的散射;而一空气柱的总散射强度<strong>并不是</strong> N 个独立分子的非相干叠加——你必须考虑这样一个事实:完全均匀的介质根本不散射,因为前向振幅恰好抵消入射波,而其余方向被相消干涉压为零。密度涨落破坏了这种抵消。</p>" },

      { en:"<p><strong>Einstein–Smoluchowski route.</strong> The mean-squared density fluctuation in a sub-volume at constant pressure is ⟨ΔN²⟩ = N k_BT κ_T / V · V = N k_BT κ_T (isothermal compressibility κ_T). Combining with the Clausius–Mossotti relation gives the differential cross-section per molecule:</p><code class="formula">dσ/dΩ = [ (2π/λ)⁴ · ((n² − 1)/(n² + 2))² · (6 + 3ρ_d)/(6 − 7ρ_d) ] · (k_BT κ_T / 9 N) · (1 + cos²θ)</code><p>or, more compactly,</p><code class="formula">dσ/dΩ = A · (1 + cos²θ),  A = [(n² − 1)² / (2 N² λ⁴)] · [(6 + 3ρ_d)/(6 − 7ρ_d)]</code><p>The (1 + cos²θ) is the classical dipole radiation pattern (Thomson-like) — symmetric front/back, minimum at θ = 90°. Integrating gives σ_total = (8π/3)A.</p>",
        zh:"<p><strong>Einstein–Smoluchowski 路线。</strong>在压强恒定的子体积内,密度涨落的均值为 ⟨ΔN²⟩ = N k_BT κ_T / V · V = N k_BT κ_T(κ_T 为等温压缩率)。结合 Clausius–Mossotti 关系,得到单个分子的微分截面:</p><code class="formula">dσ/dΩ = [ (2π/λ)⁴ · ((n² − 1)/(n² + 2))² · (6 + 3ρ_d)/(6 − 7ρ_d) ] · (k_BT κ_T / 9 N) · (1 + cos²θ)</code><p>或更紧凑地写为:</p><code class="formula">dσ/dΩ = A · (1 + cos²θ),  A = [(n² − 1)² / (2 N² λ⁴)] · [(6 + 3ρ_d)/(6 − 7ρ_d)]</code><p>其中的 (1 + cos²θ) 是经典的偶极辐射图样(类 Thomson 散射)——前后对称,在 θ = 90° 处取极小。对其积分得 σ_total = (8π/3)A。</p>" },

      { kicker:{en:"Numbers worth having",zh:"值得记住的数值"},
        en:"<ul><li>σ_Rayleigh at 550 nm ≈ 5.1 × 10⁻³¹ m² per molecule for air.</li><li>Number density at sea level N ≈ 2.5 × 10²⁵ m⁻³ → extinction coefficient β ≈ 1.3 × 10⁻⁵ m⁻¹.</li><li><strong>Optical depth</strong> τ(λ, zenith angle z) ≈ β sec z (plane-parallel), so at zenith τ(550 nm) ≈ 0.10, τ(450 nm) ≈ 0.22, τ(400 nm) ≈ 0.36, τ(650 nm) ≈ 0.05, τ(700 nm) ≈ 0.04.</li><li>Single-scattering albedo for pure Rayleigh is 1.0; real air has τ_aerosol ≈ 0.05–0.2 and O₃ absorption (Chappuis band, 450–700 nm) that mutes the red end and deepens the blue.</li></ul>",
        zh:"<ul><li>空气在 550 nm 处的瑞利散射截面 ≈ 5.1 × 10⁻³¹ m²/分子。</li><li>海平面数密度 N ≈ 2.5 × 10²⁵ m⁻³ → 消光系数 β ≈ 1.3 × 10⁻⁵ m⁻¹。</li><li><strong>光学厚度</strong> τ(λ, 天顶角 z) ≈ β sec z(平面平行近似),因此在天顶方向:τ(550 nm) ≈ 0.10,τ(450 nm) ≈ 0.22,τ(400 nm) ≈ 0.36,τ(650 nm) ≈ 0.05,τ(700 nm) ≈ 0.04。</li><li>纯瑞利散射的单次散射反照率为 1.0;真实大气中 τ_aerosol ≈ 0.05–0.2,且 O₃ 吸收(Chappuis 带,450–700 nm)会压制红端、使蓝色更纯更深。</li></ul>" },

      { kicker:{en:"Beyond the textbook λ⁻⁴ · part 1",zh:"超越教科书 λ⁻⁴ · 之一"},
        en:"<ul><li><strong>Depolarization / King's correction.</strong> Because air molecules are anisotropic (N₂ and O₂ have anisotropic polarizability tensors), incident unpolarized light produces partially polarized scattered light. The depolarization factor δ_d ≈ 0.028 for air (King correction factor (6+3δ_d)/(6−7δ_d) ≈ 1.05) — a ~5% correction you cannot get from a scalar-polarizability model.</li><li><strong>The λ⁻⁴ law is only leading order.</strong> The full refractivity dispersion (n − 1 ∝ Σ f_j/(ω_j² − ω²)) has structure from UV electronic and IR vibrational resonances; Rayleigh's own extended form (n² − 1)(n² + 2)/(6n²) replaces the simpler factor. Over 400–700 nm the effective exponent is closer to λ⁻⁴·⁰–⁴·² for air.</li></ul>",
        zh:"<ul><li><strong>退偏振 / King 修正。</strong>由于空气分子是各向异性的(N₂ 和 O₂ 的极化率是各向异性张量),入射的非偏振光会产生部分偏振的散射光。空气的退偏振因子 δ_d ≈ 0.028(King 修正因子 (6+3δ_d)/(6−7δ_d) ≈ 1.05)——这是约 5% 的修正,在标量极化率模型中无法得到。</li><li><strong>λ⁻⁴ 律只是领头阶。</strong>完整的折射率色散(n − 1 ∝ Σ f_j/(ω_j² − ω²))包含紫外电子共振和红外振动共振的结构;瑞利本人给出的推广形式 (n² − 1)(n² + 2)/(6n²) 取代了那个较简单的因子。在 400–700 nm 区间,空气的有效指数更接近 λ⁻⁴·⁰–⁴·²。</li></ul>" },

      { kicker:{en:"Beyond the textbook λ⁻⁴ · part 2",zh:"超越教科书 λ⁻⁴ · 之二"},
        en:"<ul><li><strong>Multiple scattering is not negligible.</strong> The horizon sky, and twilight generally, is dominated by 2nd- and higher-order scattering. Single-scattering Rayleigh theory predicts a horizon sky that is far too bright and too saturated; a successive-orders or radiative-transfer (RT) treatment with the full phase function P(θ) = 3/4(1 + cos²θ) is needed.</li><li><strong>Aerosols change the game.</strong> Mie scattering from accumulation-mode aerosols (x = 2πr/λ ~ 1–10) has a strongly forward-peaked phase function (g ≈ 0.6–0.8) and weak wavelength dependence, which is exactly why polluted or dusty skies go milky white/pale blue and why the corona around the Sun brightens.</li></ul>",
        zh:"<ul><li><strong>多次散射不可忽略。</strong>地平线附近的天空、以及整个暮光,都由二阶及更高阶散射主导。单次散射的瑞利理论所预测的地平线天空过亮、过饱和;需要用逐次散射法(successive orders)或带有完整相函数 P(θ) = 3/4(1 + cos²θ) 的辐射传输(RT)方法。</li><li><strong>气溶胶会改变整个局面。</strong>积聚模气溶胶(x = 2πr/λ ~ 1–10)的米氏散射具有很强的前向峰值相函数(g ≈ 0.6–0.8)且波长依赖很弱,这正是污染或有沙尘的天空呈现乳白/淡蓝、以及太阳周围日华增亮的原因。</li></ul>" },

      { kicker:{en:"Beyond the textbook λ⁻⁴ · part 3",zh:"超越教科书 λ⁻⁴ · 之三"},
        en:"<ul><li><strong>Polarization geometry.</strong> For pure single Rayleigh scattering, the degree of polarization is P = sin²θ/(1 + cos²θ), reaching P = 1 at θ = 90°. The observed “polarization neutral points” (Babinet, ~+20°, and Brewster, ~−20°, relative to the Sun) exist only because of multiple scattering — they are a clean diagnostic of aerosol optical depth and are what Haidinger's brush lets humans barely perceive.</li><li><strong>Rayleigh–Cabannes.</strong> Full treatment must sum the rotationally inelastic (rotational Raman) branches alongside the elastic Cabannes line; at low resolution this just renormalizes the total cross-section, but at high resolution (lidar, Doppler velocimetry) the rotational fine structure and the resulting Dicke/narrowing behavior matter.</li><li><strong>Why the sky isn't simply “the Sun's color, filtered.”</strong> The zenith sky's brightness is roughly (3/16)·τ·F_☉ in the single-scattering limit — blue because τ(450)/τ(650) ≈ 4.4, but its chromaticity sits near (0.17, 0.23) in CIE xy rather than deep blue, because multiple scattering and Chappuis absorption pull it back toward white.</li></ul>",
        zh:"<ul><li><strong>偏振几何。</strong>对纯单次瑞利散射,偏振度为 P = sin²θ/(1 + cos²θ),在 θ = 90° 处达到 P = 1。观测到的“偏振中性点”(Babinet 点约 +20°,Brewster 点约 −20°,均相对于太阳)只有在存在多次散射时才存在——它们是气溶胶光学厚度的良好诊断量,也是 Haidinger 刷让人类勉强能感知到的现象。</li><li><strong>Rayleigh–Cabannes 散射。</strong>完整处理必须把转动非弹性支(转动拉曼)与弹性 Cabannes 线一起求和;在低分辨率下这只是对总截面重新归一化,但在高分辨率下(激光雷达、多普勒测风)转动精细结构及其导致的 Dicke 收窄效应就变得重要。</li><li><strong>为什么天空并不是简单地“把太阳颜色滤一下”。</strong>在单次散射极限下,天顶天空的亮度约为 (3/16)·τ·F_☉ ——呈蓝色是因为 τ(450)/τ(650) ≈ 4.4,但它的色度坐标位于 CIE xy 的 (0.17, 0.23) 附近而非深蓝,这是因为多次散射和 Chappuis 吸收把它拉回了白色一侧。</li></ul>" },

      { callout:true, kicker:{en:"One-line summary",zh:"一句话总结"},
        en:"<p>The sky is blue because the atmospheric extinction optical depth scales as approximately λ⁻⁴ (Rayleigh–Cabannes scattering by sub-wavelength, polarizable, thermally fluctuating density inhomogeneities), so single-scattered sunlight viewed off the solar direction is short-wavelength dominated — with the observed hue and brightness set by the (1+cos²θ) phase function, the depolarization ratio, ozone Chappuis absorption, aerosol Mie loading, and multiple scattering.</p>",
        zh:"<p>天空之所以是蓝色的,是因为大气的消光光学厚度近似按 λ⁻⁴ 变化(由小于波长、可极化、热涨落造成的密度不均匀性引起的 Rayleigh–Cabannes 散射),因此从偏离太阳的方向观测到的单次散射阳光以短波长为主——而实际看到的色相与亮度则由 (1+cos²θ) 相函数、退偏振比、臭氧 Chappuis 吸收、气溶胶米氏散射负载以及多次散射共同决定。</p>" }
    ]
  }
